    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Welcome to Radio Curious. I'm Barry Vogel. The inner and outer workings of Congress have always intrigued me. I like to watch and talk about the process with those involved and with other observers. This week on Radio Curious, my guest will be my old law school friend, Sam Far, a member of the United States House of Representatives whose district includes Monterey and Santa Cruz counties, In this interview, we'll discuss the USA Patriot Act, the Freedom to Read Act of 2003, and the influence that the Democrats, the minority party, have in both houses of Congress. When Sam Far and I spoke on the phone a few weeks ago prior to recording this program, he talked about the political significance of the Democrats not having access to the microphone for the first time in 50 years. In this conversation, I asked him to start with that topic.",
