    "turn_text": "of the state. The Senate is a membership of 100 people. It has no rules, so each person has the ability to do whatever they want when they are recognized, and they have the microphone and they can bring up a bill, they can amend a bill, they can adjourn the house, they can do anything. So there's essentially much more of a camaraderie in the Senate to get along. There's also an ability for senators to phone in a system of holding bills from going to the floor. Each senator can block legislation from even getting considered. And so I think they respect each other's powers there and try to work out a more amicable system of allowing a fresh debate.",
