    "turn_text": "The House is certainly in Democratic control. The House has been in Democratic control for a long time, and I'm sure we abused our majority, but from what people have told me not as much as the Republicans are doing now, it's sort of get even and get, you know, it'll get bad get even and really get even. I don't know if you read the New Yorker piece on Karl Rove, but It's clear in that piece that the political strategist working for this administration by all intent purposes want to eliminate the Democratic Party from ever being able to have control of either the White House or the Senate or the House of Representatives. They've done that through reapportionment at the state level. They're doing that through trying to defeat incumbent candidates and just to make sure that anybody who thinks they can put back a democratic majority anywhere is not going to be able to make it",
