    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "That's an interesting question, because one of the things I'd like to do, I think it would shock the system, but to have every bill that's referred to a committee heard will bring in witnesses and tell the members of the committee we're going to work and we're going to vote like to do in the state legislature. you here and when i was in california legislature uh... literally thousands of bills in all the committees uh... in a year you know congress only passes probably two hundred bills maybe three hundred bills and most of those are motherhood issues naming post offices after dead congressmen and so on it's not a body that put out a lot of legislation and so therefore i think we would have the time and committees to hear a lot and that would make us more accountable on the issues but This is a town that tries to avoid you having to vote on anything controversial.",
