    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80225.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "There's a radical change in Washington and make no doubt about it. People back here feel it, sense it, and say they've never seen this much of a shift in history. And it really is boychered by the events of 9-11 which gave the President not only incredible popularity but a time of uncertainty to move legislation very rapidly uh... to give the administration not only uh... impressive authority but uh... impressive amount of money to spend on homeland defense and homeland security and in that came the adoption of the so-called patriot act uh... so-called homeland security act and others and uh... homeland security was a major reorganization of the federal government essentially put a hundred and seventy two thousand uh... federal employees under one agency and we don't even have a building to hold them uh... and moved uh... radically moved up people out of the department of agriculture out of split up by an F into uh... two different agencies and move the coast guard into homeland security and so on uh... still people are still reeling from that change back here and the president uh... with his popularity is just moving ahead to You know, push for privatization of Medicare and privatization of Social Security. I think very soon you will see voucher systems proposed in public schools in this country led by incentives given by the federal government. You know, the votes on prayer in school and today the burning, we passed a constitutional amendment today in the House of Representatives to essentially allow it to punish you for uh... desecrating the flag in the disc is that a uh... higher or maybe or maybe uh... allows congress to serve the first amendment rights of freedom of speech uh... so it's these are some really shocking things that are happening back here",
