    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, that vote came down right on partisan terms. The President Bush's appointees, which the majority of the three, voted one way and the Democratic appointees, all over from the Clinton administration, voted the other way. in the minority in this case were very very critical in fact uh... did an unusual thing of going to the press and saying how uh... sort of what a radical change this was uh... by allowing this consolidation of the media in america uh... my own district we have clear channel which owns uh... six and then control another seven radio stations now owning two out of the three local uh... tell it uh... local broadcast uh... uh... television stations so they go to their why is that why is that get dangerous it's dangerous because uh... they can go to their uh... to the people who buy the advertising which essentially runs the station and offer them packages that their competitors can offer it and a little by little you're forcing your competition out of the market uh... and that's what i think is very very dangerous you also have consolidation of that market and they can begin to interject editorial uh... opinions which then become the dominant news of the region.",
